    "Learning/Curriculum.md": {
      "path": "Learning/Curriculum.md",
      "title": "Obsidian Vault University: Curriculum & Syllabus",
      "frontmatter": {},
      "content": "# Obsidian Vault University: Curriculum & Syllabus\n## Vault: NY 17-52 Life, Accident & Health Knowledge System\n\n---\n\n### Level 0: Orientation & Vault Geography\n- **Module 0.1**: The 4-Layer Architecture (`raw/`, `wiki/`, `templates/`, `scripts/`, `AGENTS.md`).\n- **Module 0.2**: Navigation & Cataloging (`wiki/index.md`, `wiki/log.md`, `README.md`).\n- **Module 0.3**: Automated Health & Link Verification (`scripts/wiki_lint.py`).\n\n### Level 1: Foundations & Core Concepts\n- **Module 1.1**: General Insurance Principles & Contract Law (Risk, Peril, Hazard, Adhesion, Aleatory, Unilateral).\n- **Module 1.2**: Accident & Health Basics (Comprehensive vs. Limited Policies, Hospital Indemnity).\n- **Module 1.3**: Individual Health Policy Provisions (12 Mandatory, 11 Optional, Grace periods `7-10-31`, Claims `20-15-90-60-3`).\n- **Module 1.4**: Renewability Spectrum (Noncan, Guaranteed Renewable, Conditional, Optional, Cancelable).\n\n### Level 2: Practical Usage & Core Insurance Lines\n- **Module 2.1**: Managed Care & Cost Sharing (HMO, PPO, EPO, POS, D-C-C-M).\n- **Module 2.2**: Disability Income Insurance (Own Occ vs. Any Occ, Elimination & Benefit periods, BOE vs. Key Person).\n- **Module 2.3**: Group Health, COBRA & NY Continuation (Master vs. Certificate, COB Birthday Rule, 36-month NY Mini-COBRA).\n- **Module 2.4**: Federal ACA & Metal Tiers (BSGP 60-70-80-90%, 10 EHBs, $0 individual mandate penalty).\n\n### Level 3: Government Programs & Senior Products\n- **Module 3.1**: Government Programs (Medicare Parts A-D, Medicaid, SSDI).\n- **Module 3.2**: Workers' Comp vs. New York Disability Benefits Law (NY DBL $170/wk, 26 wks, 7-day wait).\n- **Module 3.3**: Long-Term Care & The 6 ADLs (BATHED, Cognitive trigger, Skilled/Intermediate/Custodial).\n- **Module 3.4**: NY State Partnership for LTC (Medicaid Total Asset Protection).\n- **Module 3.5**: Medicare Supplement (MediGap Plans A-N, NY year-round open enrollment & community rating).\n\n### Level 4: New York State Laws, Regulation & Ethics\n- **Module 4.1**: NYS DFS & Superintendent Powers (5-year examinations, hearings, fines).\n- **Module 4.2**: Producer Licensing & Maintenance (Agent vs. Broker vs. Consultant, 15-hr CE, 3-hr ethics, 30 days reporting).\n- **Module 4.3**: Unfair Trade Practices (Rebating $25 gift limit, Twisting, Defamation).\n- **Module 4.4**: Life & Health Insurance Company Guaranty Corporation of New York ($500,000 health cap, advertising ban).\n\n### Level 5: Independent Mastery & Problem Solving\n- **Module 5.1**: The 5-Step \"Strike & Solve\" Fast Question Method (72-second pacing).\n- **Module 5.2**: Wording Traps & Distractor Analysis (\"Must\" vs. \"May\", Absolute vs. Conditional).\n- **Module 5.3**: Error Logging & Knowledge Synthesis (Using `templates/template-question-error-log.md`).\n- **Module 5.4**: Independent Vault Extension (Ingesting new state circulars and updating the wiki).\n",
      "body": "# Obsidian Vault University: Curriculum & Syllabus\n## Vault: NY 17-52 Life, Accident & Health Knowledge System\n\n---\n\n### Level 0: Orientation & Vault Geography\n- **Module 0.1**: The 4-Layer Architecture (`raw/`, `wiki/`, `templates/`, `scripts/`, `AGENTS.md`).\n- **Module 0.2**: Navigation & Cataloging (`wiki/index.md`, `wiki/log.md`, `README.md`).\n- **Module 0.3**: Automated Health & Link Verification (`scripts/wiki_lint.py`).\n\n### Level 1: Foundations & Core Concepts\n- **Module 1.1**: General Insurance Principles & Contract Law (Risk, Peril, Hazard, Adhesion, Aleatory, Unilateral).\n- **Module 1.2**: Accident & Health Basics (Comprehensive vs. Limited Policies, Hospital Indemnity).\n- **Module 1.3**: Individual Health Policy Provisions (12 Mandatory, 11 Optional, Grace periods `7-10-31`, Claims `20-15-90-60-3`).\n- **Module 1.4**: Renewability Spectrum (Noncan, Guaranteed Renewable, Conditional, Optional, Cancelable).\n\n### Level 2: Practical Usage & Core Insurance Lines\n- **Module 2.1**: Managed Care & Cost Sharing (HMO, PPO, EPO, POS, D-C-C-M).\n- **Module 2.2**: Disability Income Insurance (Own Occ vs. Any Occ, Elimination & Benefit periods, BOE vs. Key Person).\n- **Module 2.3**: Group Health, COBRA & NY Continuation (Master vs. Certificate, COB Birthday Rule, 36-month NY Mini-COBRA).\n- **Module 2.4**: Federal ACA & Metal Tiers (BSGP 60-70-80-90%, 10 EHBs, $0 individual mandate penalty).\n\n### Level 3: Government Programs & Senior Products\n- **Module 3.1**: Government Programs (Medicare Parts A-D, Medicaid, SSDI).\n- **Module 3.2**: Workers' Comp vs. New York Disability Benefits Law (NY DBL $170/wk, 26 wks, 7-day wait).\n- **Module 3.3**: Long-Term Care & The 6 ADLs (BATHED, Cognitive trigger, Skilled/Intermediate/Custodial).\n- **Module 3.4**: NY State Partnership for LTC (Medicaid Total Asset Protection).\n- **Module 3.5**: Medicare Supplement (MediGap Plans A-N, NY year-round open enrollment & community rating).\n\n### Level 4: New York State Laws, Regulation & Ethics\n- **Module 4.1**: NYS DFS & Superintendent Powers (5-year examinations, hearings, fines).\n- **Module 4.2**: Producer Licensing & Maintenance (Agent vs. Broker vs. Consultant, 15-hr CE, 3-hr ethics, 30 days reporting).\n- **Module 4.3**: Unfair Trade Practices (Rebating $25 gift limit, Twisting, Defamation).\n- **Module 4.4**: Life & Health Insurance Company Guaranty Corporation of New York ($500,000 health cap, advertising ban).\n\n### Level 5: Independent Mastery & Problem Solving\n- **Module 5.1**: The 5-Step \"Strike & Solve\" Fast Question Method (72-second pacing).\n- **Module 5.2**: Wording Traps & Distractor Analysis (\"Must\" vs. \"May\", Absolute vs. Conditional).\n- **Module 5.3**: Error Logging & Knowledge Synthesis (Using `templates/template-question-error-log.md`).\n- **Module 5.4**: Independent Vault Extension (Ingesting new state circulars and updating the wiki).\n",
      "category": "Learning",
      "wordCount": 397
    },
